# Run-obeyed manifest — the single declared set of files a run loads or obeys.
#
# TWO consumers read this file and no third set exists anywhere:
#   1. scripts/check-doctrine-rev.sh  — doctrine/REV keys on the last-change
#      commit ACROSS THIS SET, never on a directory. `doctrine/` alone would
#      strand contract/journal-event.schema.json, a file a run obeys that does
#      not live under doctrine/.
#   2. scripts/check-run-context-size.sh — the size gate measures exactly this
#      set. One manifest for both is the point: a file cannot be
#      obeyed-but-unpriced or priced-but-unkeyed.
#
# ACCEPTED CONSEQUENCE, named rather than discovered later: because the two sets
# are one, editing any member — including a script's source — moves doctrine/REV
# and therefore stales every role card's `graded_under`. That is heavier coupling
# than keying on the doctrine file alone. It is deliberate: a commander that must
# read close-chain.sh to learn how to call it is obeying that file, and a grading
# cached under the old interface is stale in the way `graded_under` exists to
# express. The cost is bounded because a build re-keys once, at the end (AC-28).
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE, and why:
#   - a rationale companion file — none exists. Spec amendment A-2 withdrew it:
#     justification lives in an ADR or in the commit that makes the change.
#   - scripts/check-*.sh, scripts/test-*.sh — repo quality gates. A run never
#     calls them; they are not run-obeyed and pricing them would tax every run
#     for the repo's own hygiene.
#   - contract/fixtures/, scripts/fixtures/ — test inputs, never loaded by a run.
#   - doctrine/REV, this file — stamps and declarations about the set, not
#     members of it.
#
# Format: one repo-relative path per line. `#` comments and blank lines ignored.
# A path listed here that is missing or unreadable is a FAIL in BOTH consumers,
# never a skip and never scored as zero characters.
#
# A path prefixed `stamped ` is PRICED but NOT KEYED. Such a file carries the
# graded_under stamp that the keyed set defines, so including it in the keyed set
# is circular: re-keying it moves the very commit it was keyed to, and doctrine/
# REV is stale the instant it is written. Discovered at the first re-key under
# this manifest. The size gate measures these; the rev check skips them.

# --- L1 -----------------------------------------------------------------
doctrine/orchestration-mode.md

# --- L2: the commander<->worker interface a run obeys --------------------
contract/task-contract.md
contract/task-result.schema.json
contract/probe.schema.json
contract/journal-event.schema.json
stamped contract/roles/read-scout.md
stamped contract/roles/mech-writer.md
stamped contract/roles/fresh-verifier.md

# --- L2: source a run reads in order to call it -------------------------
contract/check-result.py
contract/check-journal-event.py
contract/make-fallback-result.py

# --- L3: adapters a run loads -------------------------------------------
adapters/claude-code/SKILL.md
adapters/claude-code/binding.md
adapters/codex/README.md
adapters/codex/binding.md

# --- source a run reads in order to call it -----------------------------
# The failing 0.7.0 arm read close-chain.sh, four audit scripts and
# probe.schema.json to learn their interfaces before calling them. That is
# product gap #6 ("腳本介面在使用點沒有文件", ~4 round-trips), and the
# 2026-07-29 replay round priced it a second time: script-source reads are
# where the two measured arms' costs diverge. A set defined only by prose files
# would score a script that grew as free.
scripts/probe-select.py
scripts/estimate-tokens.py
scripts/audit-artifact-reconciliation.py
scripts/audit-brake-lines.py
scripts/audit-judgment-flow.py
scripts/audit-model-conformance.py
scripts/audit-single-writer.sh
adapters/claude-code/tools/close-chain.sh
adapters/claude-code/tools/collect-run-stats.py
